On 2011-08-12 06.37, Dennis Boone wrote:
>   >  While each RD51 drive works correctly under the RQDX1
>   >  controller which was used to format the drive, each RD51
>   >  will not work with the other RQDX1 controller.  Each RQDX1
>   >  is able to successfully use the same RX50 floppy drive.
>
> MFM drives have always been twitchy about exchange between controllers.
> The controller defines the format, which is of course time-sensitive.
>
> My guess is winchester drives were not intended for exchange.  Since
> floppies were (and the engineering constraints were easier), they're
> working even though the MFM stuff isn't.

No. They were intended to be exchangeable. There is an explicit note for 
the RQDX3 that the format used by that controller is incompatible with 
the RQDX1 and RQDX2, so that drives are not interchangeable in this 
case. However, drives are compatible between the RQDX1 and RQDX2. As 
such, it would be very strange if they weren't interchangeable between 
two RQDX1.

However, there might be some incompatible firmware version on those 
controllers, since the RQDX1 was the first controller DEC did, and they 
might have fixed things early in the life of them that caused 
incompatibilities.

You should be able to see the firmware version using the right diagnostics.

	Johnny




