Running VMS on a Multia is not that difficult, even I managed to make
it work. My Multia came
with just 40 MB main memory IIRC and though VMS will boot and run in
that limited space it halted
within half an hour. The memory was expanded to 256 MB with memory
boards with a height that only
just fitted with the box closed. Well, you read about its cooling/
airflow issues so the memory was
reduced to 4 x 32 MB boards. It shares memory boards with the
AlphaServer 1000A 5/xxx models.
VMS was installed on a Toshiba MK1924FBV disk, at 543 MB somewhat
small.
Later on the system disk was copied to an external RZ28 drive in a
BA35x cabinet.
This works well, though its built in 10 Mb/s ethernet adapter slows it
down.
Hans


